::
Left-aligned paragraph.
::

;;
Centered paragraph, and **all Markdown inside still works**.
;;

:::
Right-aligned paragraph.
:::

;;;
Justified paragraph. This one needs enough text to actually wrap across several lines so that you can see the justification doing its work on the right-hand edge of the page, spreading the words out evenly.
;;;

Keyword form (explicit, can combine directives):

::: center
Centered with the keyword form.
:::

::: right italic
Right-aligned and in italics.
:::

## Fonts

A font block is the only way to change the font:

||font=Georgia size=13 spacing=1.6
This passage is Georgia at 13pt with a line-height of 1.6, with *italics* and **bold** still working.
||

||font=monospace
Generic families like monospace work too.
||

Blocks nest, and they flow with the text, so this is one single sentence:

||font=Georgia
It starts in Georgia,
||font=monospace
moves to monospace,
||
and returns to Georgia.
||

Only a blank line starts a new paragraph, so this one is two:

||font=Georgia
First paragraph in Georgia.

||font=monospace
Second paragraph in monospace,
||
ending in Georgia.
||

## Sizes and text formatting

Sizes by LaTeX name: [tiny]{size=tiny} [small]{size=small} [large]{size=large} [Large]{size=Large} [Huge]{size=Huge}. By points: [18pt]{size=18}. By unit: [1.5em]{size=1.5em}.

Other directives: [crimson bold]{color=#a00 bold}, [small caps, wide]{smallcaps tracking=2pt}, [underlined italic]{italic underline}, and combined: [large and brown]{size=Large color=#7a5a2f bold}.

Keyword blocks take the same directives:

::: center size=Huge bold
A Huge centered line
:::

::: right size=small italic color=#666 spacing=1.8
Small, grey, italic and widely spaced.
:::

### Heading attributes {center italic}

A trailing `{...}` styles one heading and is removed from its text and TOC entry.

### Left out of the contents {notoc color=#a00}

`notoc` hides a heading from `[TOC]`; `nolabel` skips its chapter label; `pagebreak` starts a new page before it.

